# Portfolio Project Update: Microsoft Clarity Integration

## Overview
Today, I successfully integrated **Microsoft Clarity** into my live portfolio website. This analytics tool has been set up to track, capture, and visualize user behavior, including click heatmaps, scroll depths, and complete session recordings.

> 📝 **Important Note on Historical Data:** Because tracking scripts only record live traffic, data collection begins **from today onwards**. Visitor interactions from the previous 3 months that the portfolio was online will not be retroactively reflected on the Clarity dashboard.

---

## 🛠️ Summary of Changes

### 1. Script Injection
Added the official Microsoft Clarity tracking script into the `<head>` tag of the portfolio's main HTML layout. The script initializes asynchronously to ensure that it tracks user analytics without blocking the website's initial loading speed or performance.

### 2. Feature Deployment
By deploying this integration, the portfolio now captures:
* **Session Recordings:** Playbacks of user navigation to identify friction points and layout bugs.
* **Heatmaps:** Visual click maps and scroll tracking to discover which projects or sections draw the most attention.
* **Rage Clicks & Dead Clicks:** Smart filters to catch broken links or frustrating UI elements.

---

## 🚀 Testing & Verification

To verify that the tracking code was successfully configured and operational, the following checks were performed:

1.  **Console Verification:** Opened the portfolio in an isolated environment and confirmed that the network tab successfully fires requests to Microsoft Clarity servers (`clarity.ms`) without generating console errors.
2.  **Dashboard Latency Check:** Acknowledged the normal processing buffer. Real-time metrics and session playbacks typically take anywhere from **30 minutes to 2 hours** to process and appear on the Clarity dashboard after a user terminates a session.

